  'A rigorous upper-division course in reporting, writing, producing, and presenting television, radio, streaming, and digital broadcast journalism. Students produce deadline-ready scripts, audio stories, video packages, live reports, rundowns, and a capstone portfolio while practicing verification, ethics, safety, and audience-centered distribution.',
  $brjjson${"slug": "broadcast-journalism", "title": "Broadcast Journalism", "description": "A rigorous upper-division course in reporting, writing, producing, and presenting television, radio, streaming, and digital broadcast journalism. Students produce deadline-ready scripts, audio stories, video packages, live reports, rundowns, and a capstone portfolio while practicing verification, ethics, safety, and audience-centered distribution.", "topics": [{"id": "3ee11dfa-0396-490c-9b9b-f6fd187b670e", "type": "topic", "title": "Writing for the Ear", "description": "Broadcast writing begins with language that can be understood the first time it is heard. This section trains students to write conversational, precise, tightly voiced copy that respects time, sound, and audience attention.", "children": [{"id": "7d7ffb4c-215c-42e5-8296-fb8e30bfc070", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conversational broadcast style", "children": [{"id": "976c3e46-774e-4999-b51b-5dba36284329", "type": "concept", "title": "Plain-language sentences"}, {"id": "ffb59284-9fad-4f67-a636-24f9db145b7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Active voice"}, {"id": "5d69f606-70b9-43ee-8290-6bc4244e6d42", "type": "concept", "title": "Concrete verbs"}, {"id": "a02e7898-cc43-4fe6-878a-eb9cc6b26780", "type": "concept", "title": "Read-aloud revision"}], "description": "Students learn why spoken news copy must be shorter, clearer, and more direct than print copy."}, {"id": "ff57bfb3-eed9-4075-af4a-2a5748a022d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clarity under time limits", "children": [{"id": "ab926c4c-b7f0-4d82-8d73-f272141d6135", "type": "concept", "title": "One idea per sentence"}, {"id": "a17e0855-8365-4747-bd47-e25849400662", "type": "concept", "title": "Time cues"}, {"id": "38bc549e-539d-478d-8a78-6e76b6fb2155", "type": "concept", "title": "Pronunciation checks"}, {"id": "1b6a3398-f5a9-4b8a-9007-a304e243715c", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding overloaded numbers"}], "description": "The point is to decide what the audience must know now and remove anything that slows comprehension."}, {"id": "65aaeaaa-9476-462d-9a29-b7835fde7543", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Copy for different broadcast formats", "children": [{"id": "217011e7-d588-427d-9ca7-87771548665c", "type": "concept", "title": "Reader scripts"}, {"id": "b3298324-1378-4706-9f3c-2eab83ac8ad8", "type": "concept", "title": "Voiceover copy"}, {"id": "60f90bee-6471-466d-9a51-d773469ed267", "type": "concept", "title": "Soundbite bridges"}, {"id": "b92a7660-f99c-48fb-a2a3-4924e7dec733", "type": "concept", "title": "Teases and tosses"}], "description": "Students adapt voice and structure for readers, vos, vo/sots, packages, radio wraps, podcasts, and web video."}]}, {"id": "8d5a5453-f63d-4d2f-9490-dfb17bc241e0", "type": "topic", "title": "Broadcast Story Structure and Script Formats", "description": "Broadcast stories are built through words, pictures, sound, sequencing, and timing. Students learn the professional script forms that turn reporting into clear, producible segments.", "children": [{"id": "4815af47-9863-45df-a774-4045a79b1ec3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Broadcast leads and focus", "children": [{"id": "afa0f97f-85ce-4e05-80d1-2119bf5382bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Hard-news leads"}, {"id": "358fe6e8-0d13-4e6d-a3da-6efd69cff0d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Feature leads"}, {"id": "58e08fab-110f-447f-91d5-a6a909a8ba86", "type": "concept", "title": "Nut grafs for broadcast"}, {"id": "f4fe59ae-20fa-4a8f-a51b-a838f9c843a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Localizing national stories"}], "description": "Students identify a sharp story focus and write leads that make the news value immediately audible."}, {"id": "ebfa2ce6-4454-4297-a1a3-ad6731fa9294", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Package architecture", "children": [{"id": "c1436078-9565-48d6-86c1-dc33c6aaaef2", "type": "concept", "title": "Openings"}, {"id": "2459be40-52af-437e-8e42-20dc42537aeb", "type": "concept", "title": "Setups"}, {"id": "50f25b50-9b4a-4e5e-8369-f444f08dad86", "type": "concept", "title": "Soundbite selection"}, {"id": "d0e4da74-7745-4580-8009-83d0113a19f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Track bridges"}, {"id": "1214b304-0a77-4568-b1c0-1eec15213d6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Closings"}], "description": "Students organize narration, natural sound, interviews, standups, and visual sequences into a coherent story arc."}, {"id": "e79d6005-71c4-4b6a-a2f3-6f5e999a52ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional scripting conventions", "children": [{"id": "ca32a4b1-619c-44f8-8bb9-2e6cd6e9b773", "type": "concept", "title": "Two-column scripts"}, {"id": "d3d04719-ebfe-4ca4-810b-985cdf982aea", "type": "concept", "title": "Supers and lower thirds"}, {"id": "7cbb418a-98aa-43eb-ab33-cafca0b96f2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot notes"}, {"id": "5c723215-254f-4829-a22c-30d13e005c87", "type": "concept", "title": "Timing marks"}], "description": "The goal is fluency with scripts that anchors, producers, editors, and control-room teams can actually use."}]}, {"id": "11c8b43d-5650-4ba7-8e76-a0a938e880f9", "type": "topic", "title": "Voice, Presence, and On-Air Delivery", "description": "Credible broadcast delivery combines breath, vocal control, presence, pacing, and ethical restraint. Students learn to sound natural while communicating urgency, care, and authority.", "children": [{"id": "57173ccd-863e-4747-9d25-08b2d39e50d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voice fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "3f104ba4-b799-4c98-834e-d75839544444", "type": "concept", "title": "Breath control"}, {"id": "a1adf7c6-7369-40ae-928c-6977dd44e515", "type": "concept", "title": "Pronunciation"}, {"id": "3f4796e9-25f6-457d-a5ad-7ea3b5143390", "type": "concept", "title": "Inflection"}, {"id": "527f7239-6848-43f8-9526-63436796895d", "type": "concept", "title": "Pace and pause"}], "description": "Students practice breath support, articulation, emphasis, and pacing so their delivery strengthens meaning."}, {"id": "73ec0b25-b6d8-4c57-b866-b876d248f26e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Camera and microphone presence", "children": [{"id": "f75e43ca-2f95-4ff1-9cc9-101861080c3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Eye contact"}, {"id": "10d3fb38-d377-48e2-b5fe-82dce4bcde8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Mic technique"}, {"id": "2b788c08-5313-47f3-bc1a-647a540297f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Teleprompter basics"}, {"id": "a33cfd58-680f-462f-9626-715c9cd1e720", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance anxiety routines"}], "description": "Students learn how posture, eye line, energy, and listening change across studio, field, and audio-only contexts."}, {"id": "dc18bde6-5807-41f2-8ac9-ea9fc9f1d15f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tone and credibility", "children": [{"id": "92e0943c-4eb0-4bfd-bbe8-982e8e62c6ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Breaking-news tone"}, {"id": "e0a45897-1fda-4b15-ba8d-07c502431ad0", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-sensitive delivery"}, {"id": "d83f8b30-f5c0-42b6-8085-5cc6db274722", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding performative urgency"}, {"id": "4a315b48-8b0b-4ae1-8249-53c90b81d8c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Corrections on air"}], "description": "The point is to match delivery to the subject without sensationalizing or flattening human stakes."}]}, {"id": "b2ec513b-1ab7-49c4-8dcb-4e79a9d58455", "type": "topic", "title": "Audio Reporting and Podcast Fundamentals", "description": "World-class broadcast training now requires deep audio literacy. This section builds skills in recording, writing, editing, and shaping sound-rich stories for radio, podcast, and digital listening.", "children": [{"id": "302912dd-4d81-4e60-99ab-2e08e6ba8773", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Field audio gathering", "children": [{"id": "60f07fab-d03d-4ec2-8495-ed625bd4604d", "type": "concept", "title": "Recorder settings"}, {"id": "f15c5504-c19d-4345-9179-d47acc461160", "type": "concept", "title": "Mic placement"}, {"id": "84a14569-391a-4faf-8be6-9b68d5918765", "type": "concept", "title": "Monitoring"}, {"id": "c4b11f35-d627-4782-8ca5-5c747daf5cae", "type": "concept", "title": "Room tone"}], "description": "Students learn to capture clean interviews, room tone, natural sound, ambience, and scene-setting audio."}, {"id": "27879265-4659-4cf7-b7de-2015062c7d65", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audio story craft", "children": [{"id": "46aa53f9-b1d8-44f3-8b89-eee7f419c772", "type": "concept", "title": "Actuality"}, {"id": "435d5ff2-30bf-424d-a150-91fa76f638d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Narration"}, {"id": "4b6c6052-eca2-4a88-8de2-161546445673", "type": "concept", "title": "Sound scenes"}, {"id": "19e0ca7b-a735-4ae0-a28b-2b0552a149e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Audio transitions"}], "description": "Students use sound to create structure, place, character, and evidence rather than treating audio as decoration."}, {"id": "50853aa2-f53e-4cea-a701-81f4555fc1be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Podcast formats and workflow", "children": [{"id": "30703d00-57cf-442e-b484-61fb5c8f1420", "type": "concept", "title": "Episode planning"}, {"id": "3fbfa351-bccb-48c7-80f7-669dc24789f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Host scripts"}, {"id": "c6eb6485-bd54-4762-9bdb-28274cae71b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Interview edits"}, {"id": "97844adf-e069-4eec-a0ac-38e17c702d27", "type": "concept", "title": "Series identity"}], "description": "The goal is to understand how recurring audio journalism differs from one-off radio pieces."}]}, {"id": "1fae1116-2bfb-4a43-9d12-683b115b2c15", "type": "topic", "title": "Field Reporting, Standups, and Mobile Journalism", "description": "Field reporters must gather reliable information, usable media, and audience-facing explanations in unpredictable conditions. Students learn to work safely, independently, and professionally outside the classroom newsroom.", "children": [{"id": "1892b215-a01a-4d01-bd88-325bee07d1d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Field preparation", "children": [{"id": "2d302583-8008-427b-a6d8-45a1be47fe56", "type": "concept", "title": "Pre-interviews"}, {"id": "c92ce736-d7e6-4a72-ae19-b2bc8bfc0671", "type": "concept", "title": "Location scouting"}, {"id": "843cc52c-9d9d-4da8-ae0b-298cd9f17bf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Gear checklists"}, {"id": "546cc92f-abb6-479c-be6f-5051badf0dbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety plans"}], "description": "Students plan assignments so they arrive with enough background, contacts, gear, permissions, and fallback options."}, {"id": "9c4fe878-7f8f-4f76-b3ca-52635472fdb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Standups and live shots", "children": [{"id": "e79d5279-f4c4-4b33-b142-225e4e482915", "type": "concept", "title": "Bridge standups"}, {"id": "94fb3c85-22ef-494b-a8f0-40bc7db3f67b", "type": "concept", "title": "Demonstration standups"}, {"id": "3e59442a-e9ab-4361-b7cc-787db13cfbbf", "type": "concept", "title": "Live intros"}, {"id": "85370537-f5c4-4016-97eb-a721558b2cd6", "type": "concept", "title": "Live tags"}], "description": "Students learn when reporter presence adds value and how to write standups that advance the story."}, {"id": "314c9ffd-0528-40c3-98f5-5cf71d853e32", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mobile journalism practice", "children": [{"id": "1515d58c-45a2-4618-907c-e089ed70c2aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Phone video settings"}, {"id": "6b04d637-0c9e-4cda-9fad-dfc7db9edef9", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobile audio"}, {"id": "dd2789d4-aa6a-4351-b4cd-489175e278b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Tripods and stabilization"}, {"id": "8ddfc2ff-5556-4ad0-a95f-b0ca2cd8bb92", "type": "concept", "title": "File transfer"}], "description": "The section emphasizes responsible solo reporting with phones and lightweight kits."}]}, {"id": "9d422b23-8e0a-42a4-97c4-06abb3742720", "type": "topic", "title": "Broadcast Interviewing and Source Development", "description": "Broadcast interviews must be accurate, ethical, concise, and emotionally intelligent. Students learn to prepare questions, listen actively, gather usable sound, and build sources beyond a single assignment.", "children": [{"id": "1f0eb0a2-bc9d-4331-92ec-67847d8fb0bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview preparation", "children": [{"id": "011b1b72-ae5b-4984-a912-b01b5c4eeaf1", "type": "concept", "title": "Source lists"}, {"id": "430a07a0-7d36-47d9-b199-881b6ba38544", "type": "concept", "title": "Question ladders"}, {"id": "cdaa980f-583b-41fe-b942-f5ec49733ab4", "type": "concept", "title": "Pre-interview boundaries"}, {"id": "68ffd6cc-c62f-4553-b359-800ecef2b027", "type": "concept", "title": "Document preparation"}], "description": "Students learn how background research and source mapping improve both fairness and story quality."}, {"id": "7a56a1f5-2faf-4525-b8b2-f5cef7d1ba5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "On-camera and audio interviewing", "children": [{"id": "3b6c9ac8-1845-45f6-9805-ab3e9e6f5c83", "type": "concept", "title": "Follow-up questions"}, {"id": "60dbcfa6-9c10-44f7-aaa0-dfdc4d0d90ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Silence"}, {"id": "94319311-70f5-47ec-b118-20bc19213e91", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonverbal cues"}, {"id": "e816b665-8f0a-43f8-9565-f142ce37e7d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Clean soundbites"}], "description": "Students practice asking open, direct questions while watching for quotable, truthful, and contextual answers."}, {"id": "227d5ca5-b84f-4d41-9384-8be2586920f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical source relationships", "children": [{"id": "5954be1e-e4fb-421b-93cd-86b1df7506dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Power dynamics"}, {"id": "dc5de7f6-4536-4adc-af45-eec0d59011dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed practice"}, {"id": "132d0069-af07-4855-a79d-ea8425c1b86b", "type": "concept", "title": "Vulnerable sources"}, {"id": "57d79f7d-fadc-4bdd-81d1-39205ac6b371", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency about use"}], "description": "The point is to protect independence while treating sources, victims, officials, and community members with dignity."}]}, {"id": "e6430776-54bb-4506-aea3-c8fd6c8a9785", "type": "topic", "title": "Video Shooting, Sequencing, and Editing", "description": "Strong broadcast video is reported, sequenced, and edited, not merely recorded. Students learn visual grammar, news shooting discipline, and editing choices that clarify rather than manipulate.", "children": [{"id": "c57cef51-97b0-4ff8-bc05-c3776d49e4e6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual reporting basics", "children": [{"id": "afa727e0-8241-4236-bc88-937dd8503d45", "type": "concept", "title": "Wide, medium, tight"}, {"id": "686d6d82-19b1-4117-81af-312984a0d357", "type": "concept", "title": "Action/reaction"}, {"id": "cc56651e-0999-400e-8942-7f0259615533", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutaways"}, {"id": "87d21503-cfb2-42bf-b11e-015999c62840", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequences"}], "description": "Students learn to think in shots that answer journalistic questions and show evidence."}, {"id": "5fe8e651-c3e9-4bbf-83f7-881d4f1a01a1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editing for meaning", "children": [{"id": "547d9166-2508-4906-a973-8ebe4156c23b", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot order"}, {"id": "3610ac77-c3e4-4d46-a5ae-ac7547e527d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural sound breaks"}, {"id": "30314b31-cce1-46ad-b3b6-dfe0fb9ecb9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Jump cuts"}, {"id": "92f46a38-990d-40da-9c1d-d5b2cba76b80", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding misleading edits"}], "description": "Students practice assembling video so story logic, continuity, and ethical context remain intact."}, {"id": "70c946ae-6657-48f5-9ec5-ac4a0d3b0e69", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Technical post-production", "children": [{"id": "9833a225-3369-45fc-811b-97731ba80a05", "type": "concept", "title": "Audio levels"}, {"id": "dac5d8c7-4608-4084-a446-eafed7bd695b", "type": "concept", "title": "Color correction basics"}, {"id": "392f18e1-ccf5-4998-9d7e-f64e3bce07e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Captions"}, {"id": "e7beb44d-4e65-49b5-beb5-35ae91548a0a", "type": "concept", "title": "File naming and export settings"}], "description": "The focus is on clean, deadline-ready export rather than flashy effects."}]}, {"id": "726e3e86-af00-4893-b11b-2353d46dcd6a", "type": "topic", "title": "Radio Packages, Sound Design, and Narrative Audio", "description": "Radio and audio journalism sharpen a student's ear for scene, pacing, texture, and accountability. This section explores deeper radio craft and narrative audio storytelling.", "children": [{"id": "cd5262b4-8b99-4470-9c0f-c92412b79475", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Radio package structure", "children": [{"id": "c218e746-b4d5-4f3a-b6e4-870f7dcb0d65", "type": "concept", "title": "Host ledes"}, {"id": "f696a61b-afb3-46fd-bc54-a96e8eb1a958", "type": "concept", "title": "Reporter tracks"}, {"id": "2b58a700-7a33-411f-9bab-a5a789719934", "type": "concept", "title": "Actuality selection"}, {"id": "83a6d02e-48ba-448d-b31c-d9a9e71ba1ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Tags"}], "description": "Students build wraps and features that combine narration, actuality, ambience, and clear attribution."}, {"id": "d41fe722-e6e2-4fc8-957b-d66b6fe01431", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sound design ethics", "children": [{"id": "fbda462e-dd0c-4c61-ba46-a35efbc67e0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Music boundaries"}, {"id": "9aa4ffdc-fc53-413b-8a87-092b5a9b9e96", "type": "concept", "title": "Layering ambience"}, {"id": "ec9f3836-8ee6-4273-8ec4-2a05f1ad58d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Scene transitions"}, {"id": "cb06518f-ca09-456d-ba34-9cf0386fb98d", "type": "concept", "title": "Disclosure"}], "description": "Students learn where production polish helps comprehension and where it risks distorting reality."}, {"id": "a94f4138-5764-4f48-8cd7-e6f15c0065a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Narrative pacing", "children": [{"id": "6bc61aad-4b13-4549-b1d9-427a80729193", "type": "concept", "title": "Story beats"}, {"id": "c136f4de-8a66-4c4e-b12c-47fb08159dbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Character moments"}, {"id": "4fdcc170-596f-4617-9140-b937133d9480", "type": "concept", "title": "Tension and release"}, {"id": "2c704ea6-7dd2-486e-96e2-8e632f2442c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Ending with context"}], "description": "The point is to sustain attention while keeping reporting transparent and fact-based."}]}, {"id": "5aa1cbac-8ca8-4160-97da-19b7ef6a4ef7", "type": "topic", "title": "Anchoring and Studio Performance", "description": "Anchoring is an editorial role as much as an on-camera role. Students learn to present copy, listen through the control room, recover from changes, and maintain credibility during a live show.", "children": [{"id": "acb0406a-5fca-4beb-a744-7828226c4817", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anchor copy and delivery", "children": [{"id": "74056a24-d722-4437-a776-4ac49ec099cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Script marking"}, {"id": "cd0ec8f8-6010-4a46-b5b7-6ab65f7d5731", "type": "concept", "title": "Teleprompter pacing"}, {"id": "6584c198-46bf-42ef-9537-42409665f819", "type": "concept", "title": "Ad-libbing"}, {"id": "1c2d48c0-45fc-40a5-ad87-c0a2bdf4c61f", "type": "concept", "title": "Pronunciation notes"}], "description": "Students practice marking scripts, reading cleanly, and adapting tone across story types."}, {"id": "d4f0ac1c-1679-466a-badf-27f4044b8fba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Studio mechanics", "children": [{"id": "7c4a8ece-6230-4070-b6e9-151b4ac543bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Camera blocking"}, {"id": "c7f8abd6-fceb-40c9-94a7-b8312130f35f", "type": "concept", "title": "IFB use"}, {"id": "7f51afaa-27c5-4cb9-8d42-b3dd55252a70", "type": "concept", "title": "Desk posture"}, {"id": "83b17118-b58b-4ca4-b257-0bd0f92753ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Hand-offs"}], "description": "Students learn the physical and technical routines of a live or recorded studio environment."}, {"id": "0fcf546e-4360-43fd-967d-c82ea60fe87b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editorial awareness on set", "children": [{"id": "7fcd2fc3-13c6-4faa-a2b6-c3d63d038671", "type": "concept", "title": "Corrections"}, {"id": "6ce00746-99c3-4435-ad35-1639def794a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Breaking updates"}, {"id": "4fd671e6-9dba-46ff-beb4-1040f6aeeddb", "type": "concept", "title": "Interview tosses"}, {"id": "d2258a99-87cb-4bb4-be9f-271b147ac002", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical wording"}], "description": "The goal is to remain journalistically alert rather than simply perform the rundown."}]}, {"id": "7cd316c8-f785-4515-bf3f-5798d00ef7b0", "type": "topic", "title": "Producing Rundowns, Newscasts, and Control-Room Workflow", "description": "Producing requires editorial judgment, logistics, timing, collaboration, and calm. Students learn how a newscast is planned, stacked, written, timed, changed, and executed.", "children": [{"id": "aac48b7c-f2c5-4abe-aa88-5205a4a98b11", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rundown construction", "children": [{"id": "4862148e-3794-4b85-a72a-dd74673e64f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Story stacking"}, {"id": "36d508fd-a6d0-4b8f-b263-1f5c565f1a11", "type": "concept", "title": "Teases"}, {"id": "55db8346-844c-44f8-8497-24fe8504e1bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Blocks"}, {"id": "a6f648ee-3cb5-41e9-ae98-b65977cbe74c", "type": "concept", "title": "Timing"}], "description": "Students learn to order stories with audience need, urgency, variety, geography, and available media in mind."}, {"id": "66d91d89-57f1-4850-84a1-fa69e94c79ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Control-room language", "children": [{"id": "9ca004ce-432f-495f-811d-1742d3d8b89b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cues"}, {"id": "3b94e5f9-12b4-46c3-bcb7-c81609bee3fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Counts"}, {"id": "1268bd06-1420-4983-835c-60ee1425187e", "type": "concept", "title": "Roll commands"}, {"id": "90a25ffb-cb09-4104-bd29-25e5547a14e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Communication discipline"}], "description": "Students gain working vocabulary for directors, technical directors, audio, graphics, floor, anchors, and reporters."}, {"id": "2cd063b6-bf87-4cbe-b0ef-1abf7239cb79", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editorial producing", "children": [{"id": "67b736fa-948e-411a-8467-2f5d1fb28a42", "type": "concept", "title": "Story selection"}, {"id": "93d37ea9-7a1f-4fb2-9033-1d035167edef", "type": "concept", "title": "Updates"}, {"id": "7b3bf434-b1d4-43fd-a9f5-25aaf281d9f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Push alerts"}, {"id": "fedac6a1-da65-4916-9c52-32ab2a674c59", "type": "concept", "title": "Show debriefs"}], "description": "The focus is on making fast decisions without abandoning verification or proportion."}]}, {"id": "e83945ad-0827-4a95-8284-f95814175a30", "type": "topic", "title": "Live Reporting, Breaking News, and Verification", "description": "Live journalism tests every habit in the course. Students learn to report what is known, explain what is unknown, verify before amplifying, and keep audiences informed without speculation.", "children": [{"id": "4af038a2-bcb9-491e-bea3-5fb51e3d4780", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Breaking-news discipline", "children": [{"id": "b81c3690-ee55-47d0-a16e-670ba54ef2f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Attribution tiers"}, {"id": "263ffd90-45bf-48c3-97fb-b90f55dfbbd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Unconfirmed information"}, {"id": "0abe1b99-4650-4bcf-93f0-0332f0c6cd10", "type": "concept", "title": "Official sources"}, {"id": "da8dd99c-6a6c-4c58-b19a-f2336265a6c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Corrections"}], "description": "Students practice language and workflows that separate confirmed facts from reports, claims, context, and analysis."}, {"id": "f878af5b-3db1-4713-bb1b-82c2d616a55b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Live field workflow", "children": [{"id": "1c7d8c9c-c4fe-45d5-9b1a-5742a5b83ece", "type": "concept", "title": "Live intros"}, {"id": "948f3ed2-2581-4d06-915d-608a37652c99", "type": "concept", "title": "Look-lives"}, {"id": "65f17351-2bdf-470b-b614-e8a25008b232", "type": "concept", "title": "IFB communication"}, {"id": "0ccf4374-4f18-48d3-832a-0c8ff9ec5bf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Scene safety"}], "description": "Students learn how to prepare live hits, coordinate with producers, and update safely from the scene."}, {"id": "29a6ebdb-bcf9-423e-a665-4a371e5cb085", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Verification under pressure", "children": [{"id": "2a55f095-ec51-4469-9292-48be58b335f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Reverse image search"}, {"id": "c7078578-dda3-4c94-995e-1ed841889f23", "type": "concept", "title": "Geolocation basics"}, {"id": "d2bfa12e-36c4-4c76-b091-80eec85b7730", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata limits"}, {"id": "0db395db-0eb6-4f40-8d74-a42aae46d80b", "type": "concept", "title": "Crowdsourced material"}], "description": "The point is to build reflexes for checking images, video, claims, locations, times, and identities before publication."}]}, {"id": "d7b38f7a-a907-4b35-b8e7-0d535684f0ae", "type": "topic", "title": "Broadcast Ethics, Law, Standards, and Safety", "description": "Broadcast journalism carries high risks because images, sound, speed, and emotion can shape public understanding immediately. Students learn legal boundaries, newsroom standards, and practical safety routines.", "children": [{"id": "0f9cd08d-dbf4-481b-9143-c4619315e1c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics and editorial standards", "children": [{"id": "b8d2f1e9-2457-44bd-87ec-e40c2e36486d", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphic content"}, {"id": "2365d76f-30e4-4fe5-8160-42b29e4dbc08", "type": "concept", "title": "Victim identification"}, {"id": "9f5c295a-b8fd-4c01-acc7-445ee02468dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Staging and reenactment"}, {"id": "06d5a184-95d3-4801-b792-3e1d1a9a5c6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicts of interest"}], "description": "Students apply truth, independence, minimization of harm, accountability, and transparency to broadcast-specific dilemmas."}, {"id": "e581daa5-1cad-4287-a0c9-7baf5c46be1b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media law for broadcast", "children": [{"id": "de468bf5-dd37-4566-b5d1-2de42927ab8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Libel"}, {"id": "89bd26da-e13e-4f14-a620-504d4e588492", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy"}, {"id": "c30da755-4327-4e31-9626-5d765d89cfe0", "type": "concept", "title": "Copyright/fair use"}, {"id": "a9f4bfdf-abb7-4a4b-8ff2-7bd7ffa38666", "type": "concept", "title": "Recording consent"}], "description": "Students learn core legal concepts that affect scripts, visuals, access, recording, and publication."}, {"id": "22109c03-28d5-4157-bec8-5a47a641d75a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reporter safety", "children": [{"id": "764bb2ce-b4ef-4af6-a786-471a73efaa2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Protests"}, {"id": "ed028943-5c55-4757-a3e8-8aa43e67757d", "type": "concept", "title": "Severe weather"}, {"id": "92ef93ac-ee93-4dc8-9cce-5e6aa9a15e91", "type": "concept", "title": "Crime scenes"}, {"id": "0977b420-9c28-429c-abc9-a7a7359d7a8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital harassment"}], "description": "The goal is to prepare students to assess risk before and during field work."}]}, {"id": "f7c61627-ce74-4db5-9d0c-f1e4cadeffe3", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Distribution, Social Video, Accessibility, and Analytics", "description": "Broadcast stories now travel across television, radio, streaming, social platforms, newsletters, websites, and apps. Students learn to publish responsibly for different formats while keeping accessibility and audience service central.", "children": [{"id": "6c30812b-73f9-4257-855b-958e5a1b7b6c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Platform adaptation", "children": [{"id": "61f2abc0-f403-4ad6-90af-b929e6cdfc6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Vertical video"}, {"id": "07d0fcce-38b4-40d7-b76f-d5e89b8a3941", "type": "concept", "title": "Thumbnails"}, {"id": "3dced4ec-4763-4529-960e-5bfbcd55d161", "type": "concept", "title": "SEO headlines"}, {"id": "30290358-51c7-444c-a36b-f1aa71157ef8", "type": "concept", "title": "Platform-native captions"}], "description": "Students recut and rewrite broadcast work for social video, web embeds, reels, newsletters, and streaming clips."}, {"id": "f4ea6965-6916-4947-b3d3-2ce520b811bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility and inclusive production", "children": [{"id": "0f91c231-e12f-407a-b861-b4e2d24a408f", "type": "concept", "title": "Closed captions"}, {"id": "c280b20e-67a9-4692-8d36-1b83af84fbee", "type": "concept", "title": "Audio clarity"}, {"id": "9b4253b0-adb3-4677-b0be-9cce748e8b94", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text"}, {"id": "b3e38d4f-5bae-477d-b009-96be779001ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Names and pronunciation"}], "description": "Students learn that accessibility is a journalistic quality standard, not a final technical chore."}, {"id": "9a7ad673-217b-4bd3-81d4-c75e399c8254", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audience analytics", "children": [{"id": "47a48ee9-e754-4c55-87a3-da37e22cbf69", "type": "concept", "title": "Watch time"}, {"id": "0ce46ac7-575e-442e-b7d8-279a80eb2fab", "type": "concept", "title": "Retention"}, {"id": "a0962318-b09c-44bd-ac0a-aeff46d132b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Referral sources"}, {"id": "0014577a-d0b3-4796-b8ac-93eedefc10cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Impact signals"}], "description": "The point is to use metrics as feedback without letting metrics replace public-service judgment."}]}, {"id": "3716c97b-7d24-4d94-a794-c4219f5bb491", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone Package and Newsroom Simulation", "description": "The course culminates in newsroom-quality work that demonstrates reporting, writing, production, delivery, ethics, and revision. Students finish with portfolio pieces and a clearer sense of professional standards.", "children": [{"id": "5d18d251-335f-4e80-b5f5-9f571fda6505", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Enterprise broadcast package", "children": [{"id": "df22aac8-870f-4ee0-b7f3-0c49816f65a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Pitch memo"}, {"id": "cb44f5a8-9f52-42f4-888f-0bf671bef7fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Reporting plan"}, {"id": "e8c2612e-4618-4642-a616-3ed298c10303", "type": "concept", "title": "Rough cut"}, {"id": "e99b843f-7787-4605-80bf-b84d74a0533f", "type": "concept", "title": "Final package"}], "description": "Students produce a complete reported package or audio/video feature with a strong focus and multiple sources."}, {"id": "ace3b171-30c6-4430-8a65-70114d0e2cc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Live or studio simulation", "children": [{"id": "c5d92cd7-962e-4b05-aac9-8703bd4faaf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Rundown roles"}, {"id": "348a33d7-799e-4645-9e64-3a83a227a7af", "type": "concept", "title": "Anchor/reporter handoffs"}, {"id": "6c244d2b-8fb4-42ce-8d16-d8350f9bc714", "type": "concept", "title": "Last-minute updates"}, {"id": "76299cc3-83a0-48b3-8311-1d9dfa250d9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-show critique"}], "description": "Students participate in a timed show environment that requires teamwork, adjustment, and control-room discipline."}, {"id": "3a65cd10-05bd-486e-9bae-4a1a846b7603", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio and reflection", "children": [{"id": "6e63a61c-8abc-4f95-832e-7205bf1541b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Revised scripts"}, {"id": "99166bac-a89e-4c91-bd68-1f41aa3e1c44", "type": "concept", "title": "Final exports"}, {"id": "4e0ff7af-2b88-4699-8e18-be22674ad546", "type": "concept", "title": "Process memo"}, {"id": "12f6f7b1-dc42-4e3a-a18e-faa3f6c960ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Demo reel selection"}], "description": "The goal is to connect craft growth to employable evidence and ethical self-assessment."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$brjjson$::jsonb,
